  "caption": "Nurse Quinn's 12-hour shift: plenty of steps, plenty of coffee. Then a patient slipped, Quinn grabbed without a hoist or a second person, and the back filed a complaint. Day-sleep didn't help.\n\nPatient handling is unpredictable load, and long shifts, prolonged standing and broken sleep add up. Standing all day doesn't build the strength that lifting needs.\n\nWhat can help: using hoists and slide sheets every time, even when rushed, getting a second pair of hands for unplanned transfers, two short strength sessions a week, good footwear and changing position during long standing, and protecting sleep between shifts.\n\nIf your back is sore most shifts or the same flare keeps returning, get it assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
